#@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#@ Scratch file for the user's own host entries.  mu2e-ssh-setup creates this
#@ only if it does not already exist, and never overwrites it.
#@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private host entries -- this file is yours.
#
# mu2e-ssh-setup created this file because it did not exist.  It will never
# overwrite it, so anything you add here survives regenerating the rest of the
# Mu2e configuration.
#
# Remember that ssh takes the FIRST value it finds for each keyword.  Because
# this file is included last, a setting here will NOT override one made by an
# earlier Mu2e host group.  If you need to override a Mu2e default, ask
# mu2e-ssh-setup to put this file first (--user-config-first).
#
# Example:
#
# Host mylaptop
#         HostName        192.168.1.20
#         User            @@LOCAL_USER@@
#         ForwardX11      no
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
